 "intro": "A feeling about what another person does takes the subjunctive, even when the fact is true.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "me alegro de que",
   "significado": "I'm glad that",
   "pron": "me a-LE-gro de ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has «de» before «que». You can also say «me alegra que», without «de».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "qué pena que",
   "significado": "what a pity that",
   "pron": "ke PE-na ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is an exclamation. It has no «me»: «¡qué pena que no vengas!». It ends in the subjunctive.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "siento que",
   "significado": "I'm sorry that",
   "pron": "SYEN-to ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Here «sentir» means to regret, not to notice. «Siento que no puedas venir» is an apology.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "me molesta que",
   "significado": "it bothers me that",
   "pron": "me mo-LES-ta ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "What bothers is what comes after «que», so «molesta» stays singular.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "me encanta que",
   "significado": "I love it that",
   "pron": "me en-KAN-ta ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Stronger than «me gusta que». Both ask for the subjunctive if the person changes.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "me sorprende que",
   "significado": "it surprises me that",
   "pron": "me sor-PREN-de ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It works for good and bad surprises. The fact can be true: it still takes the subjunctive.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "me da miedo que",
   "significado": "I'm afraid that",
   "pron": "me da MYE-do ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You use «dar miedo», not «tener miedo»: «me da miedo que llegues tarde».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "me extraña que",
   "significado": "I find it odd that",
   "pron": "me eks-TRA-nya ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The ñ sounds «ny»: «eks-TRA-nya». Do not mix it up with «extranjero».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "qué bien que",
   "significado": "how great that",
   "pron": "ke byen ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A short, very common exclamation: «¡qué bien que vengas!».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "qué raro que",
   "significado": "how strange that",
   "pron": "ke RA-ro ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It expresses surprise: «¡qué raro que no llame!». It also takes the subjunctive.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "puntual",
   "significado": "punctual",
   "pron": "pun-TWAL",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It works for a man and a woman. The opposite is «impuntual». Say «pun-TWAL».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "gente",
   "significado": "people",
   "pron": "HEN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
