   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Feeling something about what another does",
     "texto": [
      "When a sentence expresses a **feeling** and what causes it is done by **another person**, the verb goes in the **subjunctive**:\n\n- **Me alegro de que** estés aquí.\n- ¡**Qué pena que** no puedas venir!\n- **Me molesta que** fumen.\n- **Me extraña que** no llame.\n\nThe fact can be **true**: you are here, they smoke. You use the subjunctive because you **react** to the fact; you are not reporting it.\n\nIf the one who feels and the one who acts are the **same person**, use the infinitive: **me alegro de estar** aquí, **siento llegar** tarde."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Three families of feelings",
     "texto": [
      "Feeling expressions group like this:\n\n- **Joy and liking**: me alegro de que · me alegra que · me encanta que · me gusta que · qué bien que.\n- **Sadness, annoyance and fear**: siento que · qué pena que · me molesta que · me da miedo que.\n- **Surprise**: me sorprende que · me extraña que · qué raro que.\n\nThey all follow the same pattern: **feeling + que + subjunctive** if the subject changes, and **feeling + infinitive** if the subject is the same.\n\nWatch the preposition: **alegrarse de** (me alegro de que), but **me alegra que**, without «de»."
     ],
